    "answer": {
      "short": "Sample pictogram shown, with one symbol representing 10 large cats: Tiger 7 symbols, Lion 10, Jaguar 4, Cheetah 5, Puma 3.",
      "worked": "Use equal-sized symbols and a key of one symbol for 10 large cats.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Tiger symbols}&=70\\div10=7\\\\\\text{Lion symbols}&=100\\div10=10\\\\\\text{Jaguar symbols}&=40\\div10=4\\\\\\text{Cheetah symbols}&=50\\div10=5\\\\\\text{Puma symbols}&=30\\div10=3\\end{align*}$$\n\nDraw the labelled rows with these numbers of symbols and include the title and key.",
      "solutionDiagrams": [
        {
          "id": "p8-q4-solution-pictogram",
          "role": "solution",
          "format": "tikz",
          "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 8 question 4; teacher page 60\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont},line width=0.8pt]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\node[anchor=west] at (-2,0.8) {Large cat numbers at an open range zoo};\n\\foreach \\name/\\y/\\n in {Tiger/0/7,Lion/-1/10,Jaguar/-2/4,Cheetah/-3/5,Puma/-4/3}{\n\\node[anchor=east] at (-0.4,\\y) {\\name};\n\\foreach \\i in {1,...,\\n}{\\draw ({0.7*(\\i-1)},\\y) circle[radius=0.18];}\n}\n\\draw (0,-5) circle[radius=0.18];\n\\node[anchor=west] at (0.4,-5) {$=10$ large cats};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
